   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the disposition of\nexcess funds of the municipal assistance corporation for the city of Troy and\nproviding for the termination of the municipal assistance corporation for the\ncity of Troy",
    "basePrintNo": "S6441",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6441-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3053, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6441\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the disposi-\ntion of excess funds of the municipal assistance corporation for the\ncity of Troy and providing for the termination of the municipal assist-\nance corporation for the city of Troy\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe City of Troy Municipal Assistance Corporation will dissolve after\nthe final payment in January 2022. To allow the assets that remain to be\ntransferred to the City of Troy, this legislative change is necessary.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 3053 of the public authorities law to add a new\nsubdivision 1-a to correct the Municipal Assistance Corporation (MAC)\nlaw for the City of Troy to allow the remaining assets in the City of\nTroy MAC to revert to the City rather than the State when the MAC\ndissolves.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
